-- Regulation W, 12 CFR 223.3(h), (i), (a), 223.11, 223.12, 223.16: what is a covered transaction,
-- what is treated as one, and the two quantitative limits.
--
-- Target compiler: main (see NOTES.md).
-- Who is an affiliate comes from regw-affiliate.l4 (12 CFR 223.2), for the purposes of section 23A.
-- Amounts are plain numbers in one currency unit and are compared exactly.
-- Each function answers for one instant from the facts stated to it, including the amount of the
-- covered transactions already outstanding and the member bank's capital stock and surplus
-- (223.3(d)), which is a stated number.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `regw-nouns`
IMPORT `regw-control`
IMPORT `regw-affiliate`
IMPORT `regwb-nouns`

§ `223.3(h) and (i): covered transactions and credit transactions`

-- 223.3(i): "Credit transaction with an affiliate means: (1) An extension of credit to the affiliate;
-- (2) An issuance of a guarantee, acceptance, or letter of credit ... on behalf of the affiliate and a
-- confirmation of a letter of credit issued by the affiliate; and (3) A cross-affiliate netting arrangement."
GIVEN k IS A `Transaction kind`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@ref 12 CFR 223.3(i)
`is a credit transaction kind` MEANS
       k EQUALS `An extension of credit`
    OR k EQUALS `The issuance of a guarantee, acceptance or letter of credit, or the confirmation of a letter of credit`
    OR k EQUALS `A cross-affiliate netting arrangement`

-- 223.3(h)(1) to (5): the kinds of transaction that are covered when they are with, or concern, an affiliate.
GIVEN k IS A `Transaction kind`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@ref 12 CFR 223.3(h)
`is a kind of covered transaction` MEANS NOT (k EQUALS `Some other transaction`)

-- 223.3(h): "Covered transaction with respect to an affiliate means: ...".  The affiliate is judged for
-- the purposes of section 23A (223.2(c) takes depository institutions out of "affiliate" for subpart F only).
-- (h)(3) leaves out "such purchases of real and personal property as may be specifically exempted by the Board".
GIVEN
    s IS A Structure
    r IS A Readings
    t IS A Transaction
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@ref 12 CFR 223.3(h)
`is a covered transaction` MEANS
        `is a kind of covered transaction` (t's `kind`)
    AND `is an affiliate` s r `Section 23A` (t's `affiliate concerned`)
    AND (NOT (t's `kind` EQUALS `A purchase of an asset` AND t's `exempted by the Board as a purchase of property`))

§ `223.3(a): the aggregate amount`

-- "Aggregate amount of covered transactions means the amount of the covered transaction about to be
-- engaged in added to the current amount of all outstanding covered transactions."
GIVEN
    about       IS A NUMBER
    outstanding IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
@ref 12 CFR 223.3(a)
`aggregate amount of covered transactions` MEANS about PLUS outstanding

-- "would exceed N percent of the capital stock and surplus": exactly, with no rounding.
GIVEN
    aggregate IS A NUMBER
    css       IS A NUMBER
    percent   IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`exceeds a percent of capital stock and surplus` MEANS aggregate TIMES 100 GREATER THAN css TIMES percent

§ `223.11 and 223.12: the limits`

GIVEN
    s    IS A Structure
    name IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`names a financial subsidiary` MEANS
    any (GIVEN q YIELD q's `name` EQUALS name AND q's `is a financial subsidiary`) (s's `the parties`)

-- 223.11: "A member bank may not engage in a covered transaction with an affiliate (other than a
-- financial subsidiary of the member bank) if the aggregate amount of the member bank's covered
-- transactions with such affiliate would exceed 10 percent of the capital stock and surplus of the
-- member bank."  `outstanding` is the current amount of the outstanding covered transactions with
-- that affiliate.
GIVEN
    s           IS A Structure
    r           IS A Readings
    t           IS A Transaction
    outstanding IS A NUMBER
    css         IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@ref 12 CFR 223.11
`would breach the single-affiliate limit` MEANS
        `is a covered transaction` s r t
    AND (NOT (`names a financial subsidiary` s (t's `affiliate concerned`)))
    AND `exceeds a percent of capital stock and surplus` (`aggregate amount of covered transactions` (t's `value`) outstanding) css 10

-- 223.12: "A member bank may not engage in a covered transaction with any affiliate if the aggregate
-- amount of the member bank's covered transactions with all affiliates would exceed 20 percent of the
-- capital stock and surplus of the member bank."  `outstanding` is the current amount of the
-- outstanding covered transactions with all affiliates.
GIVEN
    s           IS A Structure
    r           IS A Readings
    t           IS A Transaction
    outstanding IS A NUMBER
    css         IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@ref 12 CFR 223.12
`would breach the all-affiliates limit` MEANS
        `is a covered transaction` s r t
    AND `exceeds a percent of capital stock and surplus` (`aggregate amount of covered transactions` (t's `value`) outstanding) css 20

§ `223.16: transactions treated as transactions with an affiliate`

-- (a): "A member bank must treat any of its transactions with any person as a transaction with an
-- affiliate to the extent that the proceeds of the transaction are used for the benefit of, or
-- transferred to, an affiliate."
-- (b)(1): an extension of credit to a nonaffiliate is not so treated if "(i) The proceeds ... are used
-- to purchase an asset through an affiliate of the member bank, and the affiliate is acting exclusively
-- as an agent or broker in the transaction; and (ii) The asset purchased by the nonaffiliate is not
-- issued, underwritten, or sold as principal by any affiliate of the member bank."
-- (b)(2): that "does not apply to the extent of any agency fee, brokerage commission, or other
-- compensation received by an affiliate from the proceeds".
-- The amount returned is the part of the transaction treated as a transaction with an affiliate.
GIVEN
    t IS A Transaction
    u IS A `Use of proceeds`
GIVETH A NUMBER
@ref 12 CFR 223.16(a)
@ref 12 CFR 223.16(b)
`amount treated as a transaction with an affiliate` MEANS
    IF agencyExceptionApplies
    THEN min (u's `agency fee, brokerage commission or other compensation an affiliate receives from the proceeds`) (t's `value`)
    ELSE min (u's `amount used for the benefit of, or transferred to, an affiliate`) (t's `value`)
    WHERE
        agencyExceptionApplies MEANS
                t's `kind` EQUALS `An extension of credit`
            AND u's `used to purchase an asset through an affiliate acting exclusively as agent or broker`
            AND u's `asset not issued, underwritten or sold as principal by any affiliate`
